{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NquCo6XgsasbsmPQqiC7jv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Architecture Chat\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→Replace the subprocess-based CLI chat with two first-class provider backends:\n     6→1. **Claude** via Companion fork's WebSocket bridge (`vista/companion/`)\n     7→2. **OpenCode** via `opencode serve` HTTP REST + SSE streaming\n     8→\n     9→Vista's FastAPI server remains the single hub. The existing Jinja2/vanilla JS frontend is kept; Companion's React UI is NOT used.\n    10→\n    11→---\n    12→\n    13→## Phase 1: Service Lifecycle Manager\n    14→\n    15→**Goal**: Auto-start/stop/restart Companion and OpenCode alongside the Vista FastAPI server.\n    16→\n    17→### New File: `server/services/service_lifecycle.py`\n    18→\n    19→A `ServiceLifecycleManager` class managing named service instances:\n    20→\n    21→```\n    22→ServiceInstance:\n    23→  name: str              # \"companion\" | \"opencode\"\n    24→  command: list[str]     # e.g. [\"bun\", \"web/server/index.ts\"]\n    25→  cwd: str               # working directory\n    26→  port: int              # assigned port\n    27→  health_url: str        # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/sessions\"\n    28→  status: str            # stopped | starting | running | error | restarting\n    29→  pid: int | None\n    30→  process: Popen | None\n    31→  started_at: float | None\n    32→  restart_count: int\n    33→  max_restarts: int      # default 5\n    34→  backoff_seconds: float  # exponential: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (capped)\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→**State machine** (matches `state-service-lifecycle.mmd`):\n    38→- `Stopped -> Starting -> Running -> Stopping -> Stopped`\n    39→- `Running -> Error -> Restarting -> Starting`\n    40→- `Error -> Stopped` (max retries exceeded)\n    41→\n    42→**Methods**:\n    43→- `start(name)` — spawn process, wait for health\n    44→- `stop(name)` — graceful terminate, force kill after 5s\n    45→- `restart(name)` — stop then start\n    46→- `health_check(name)` — HTTP GET to health_url\n    47→- `start_all()` — called from `app_lifespan` or `mcp_server.app_lifespan`\n    48→- `stop_all()` — called on shutdown\n    49→- `get_status(name)` — return ServiceInstance snapshot\n    50→- `get_all_status()` — return all services\n    51→\n    52→**Periodic health checker**: asyncio task, every 10s, 3 consecutive failures triggers restart with backoff.\n    53→\n    54→**Integration points**:\n    55→- `server/app.py` lifespan: call `lifecycle.start_all()` on startup, `lifecycle.stop_all()` on shutdown\n    56→- `mcp_server.py` lifespan: also calls `lifecycle.start_all()` so services start regardless of entry point\n    57→\n    58→### Companion Service Config\n    59→\n    60→```python\n    61→ServiceConfig(\n    62→    name=\"companion\",\n    63→    command=[\"bun\", \"web/server/index.ts\"],\n    64→    cwd=str(PLUGIN_ROOT / \"companion\" / \"web\"),\n    65→    preferred_port=3457,\n    66→    health_url=\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/sessions\",\n    67→    env={\"NODE_ENV\": \"production\", \"PORT\": \"{port}\"},\n    68→)\n    69→```\n    70→\n    71→**Prerequisites check**: `shutil.which(\"bun\")` — if not found, skip Companion startup and disable Claude provider.\n    72→\n    73→### OpenCode Service Config\n    74→\n    75→```python\n    76→ServiceConfig(\n    77→    name=\"opencode\",\n    78→    command=[\"opencode\", \"serve\", \"--port\", \"{port}\"],\n    79→    preferred_port=4096,\n    80→    health_url=\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/global/health\",\n    81→)\n    82→```\n    83→\n    84→**Prerequisites check**: `shutil.which(\"opencode\")` — if not found, skip OpenCode startup and disable OpenCode provider.\n    85→\n    86→### Changes to Existing Files\n    87→\n    88→| File | Change |\n    89→|------|--------|\n    90→| `server/app.py` | Import lifecycle manager, call `start_all()`/`stop_all()` in lifespan |\n    91→| `server/config.py` | Add `get_chat_settings()` returning companion/opencode port config |\n    92→| `mcp_server.py` | Remove inline `_start_opencode_serve()`, delegate to lifecycle manager |\n    93→\n    94→### New Route: `server/routes/service_status.py`\n    95→\n    96→```\n    97→GET /api/services/health → {services: [{name, port, status, uptime, pid}]}\n    98→```\n    99→\n   100→### Tests: `tests/test_service_lifecycle.py`\n   101→\n   102→TDD candidate. Test state transitions, backoff calculation, max retry cap.\n   103→\n   104→---\n   105→\n   106→## Phase 2: Provider Router (Claude WebSocket + OpenCode SSE)\n   107→\n   108→**Goal**: Replace the subprocess-based `ChatService` with protocol-native provider backends.\n   109→\n   110→### New File: `server/services/provider_router.py`\n   111→\n   112→```python\n   113→class ProviderRouter:\n   114→    \"\"\"Routes chat messages to the correct backend based on provider type.\"\"\"\n   115→\n   116→    async def send_message(\n   117→        self,\n   118→        provider: str,       # \"claude\" | \"opencode\"\n   119→        model: str,\n   120→        prompt: str,          # fully assembled prompt\n   121→        session_id: str,      # Vista's session ID\n   122→        cwd: str,             # project root for Claude CLI\n   123→    ) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n   124→        \"\"\"Yield streaming events: {type: \"token\"|\"done\"|\"error\", ...}\"\"\"\n   125→        if provider == \"claude\":\n   126→            async for event in self._send_claude(model, prompt, session_id, cwd):\n   127→                yield event\n   128→        elif provider == \"opencode\":\n   129→            async for event in self._send_opencode(model, prompt, session_id):\n   130→                yield event\n   131→        else:\n   132→            yield {\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": f\"Unknown provider: {provider}\"}\n   133→```\n   134→\n   135→### Claude Provider: WebSocket Bridge to Companion\n   136→\n   137→**New File**: `server/services/claude_ws_client.py`\n   138→\n   139→```python\n   140→class ClaudeWSClient:\n   141→    \"\"\"WebSocket client connecting to Companion's /ws/browser/{session_id} endpoint.\"\"\"\n   142→\n   143→    def __init__(self, companion_url: str):\n   144→        self.companion_url = companion_url  # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:3457\"\n   145→        self._ws = None\n   146→        self._session_id = None\n   147→\n   148→    async def create_session(self, model: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n   149→        \"\"\"POST /api/sessions/create → returns Companion session ID.\n   150→\n   151→        Companion spawns Claude CLI with --sdk-url, --dangerously-skip-permissions,\n   152→        --model, --verbose, --output-format stream-json.\n   153→        \"\"\"\n   154→        ...\n   155→\n   156→    async def connect(self, session_id: str):\n   157→        \"\"\"Connect to ws://{companion_url}/ws/browser/{session_id}\"\"\"\n   158→        ...\n   159→\n   160→    async def send_message(self, text: str) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n   161→        \"\"\"Send user message and yield streaming events.\n   162→\n   163→        Send: {\"type\": \"user\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}}\n   164→\n   165→        Receive and translate:\n   166→        - {\"type\": \"stream_event\", \"event\": {\"type\": \"content_block_delta\",\n   167→           \"delta\": {\"text\": \"tok\"}}} → {\"type\": \"token\", \"text\": \"tok\"}\n   168→        - {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": ...} → {\"type\": \"done\", \"content\": \"...\"}\n   169→        - {\"type\": \"result\", ...} → {\"type\": \"result\", ...}\n   170→        - {\"type\": \"permission_request\", ...} → auto-approve immediately\n   171→        \"\"\"\n   172→        ...\n   173→\n   174→    async def disconnect(self):\n   175→        \"\"\"Close WebSocket connection.\"\"\"\n   176→        ...\n   177→\n   178→    async def delete_session(self, session_id: str):\n   179→        \"\"\"DELETE /api/sessions/{session_id}\"\"\"\n   180→        ...\n   181→```\n   182→\n   183→Uses `websockets` library (async WebSocket client for Python). Add to dependencies.\n   184→\n   185→**Permission auto-approve**: If a `permission_request` arrives (shouldn't normally with `--dangerously-skip-permissions`), respond with:\n   186→```json\n   187→{\"type\": \"permission_response\", \"request_id\": \"...\", \"behavior\": \"allow\", \"updated_input\": {...}}\n   188→```\n   189→\n   190→### OpenCode Provider: HTTP REST + SSE\n   191→\n   192→**New File**: `server/services/opencode_client.py`\n   193→\n   194→```python\n   195→class OpenCodeClient:\n   196→    \"\"\"Async client for OpenCode's REST API + SSE streaming.\"\"\"\n   197→\n   198→    def __init__(self, base_url: str):\n   199→        self.base_url = base_url  # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:4096\"\n   200→\n   201→    async def create_session(self, title: str) -> str:\n   202→        \"\"\"POST /session → returns session ID\"\"\"\n   203→        ...\n   204→\n   205→    async def send_message_streaming(\n   206→        self, session_id: str, text: str, model: dict | None = None\n   207→    ) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n   208→        \"\"\"POST /session/{id}/prompt_async, then subscribe to GET /event SSE.\n   209→\n   210→        Translate events:\n   211→        - event: message.part.updated → {\"type\": \"token\", \"text\": delta}\n   212→        - event: session.idle → {\"type\": \"done\", \"content\": full_text}\n   213→        - event: session.error → {\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": msg}\n   214→        \"\"\"\n   215→        ...\n   216→\n   217→    async def get_providers(self) -> list[dict]:\n   218→        \"\"\"GET /config/providers → provider/model list for model selection\"\"\"\n   219→        ...\n   220→\n   221→    async def delete_session(self, session_id: str):\n   222→        \"\"\"DELETE /session/{id}\"\"\"\n   223→        ...\n   224→\n   225→    async def abort_session(self, session_id: str):\n   226→        \"\"\"POST /session/{id}/abort\"\"\"\n   227→        ...\n   228→```\n   229→\n   230→Uses `httpx` for async HTTP and SSE (via `httpx-sse`). Add to dependencies.\n   231→\n   232→### Session Mapping\n   233→\n   234→The ProviderRouter maintains a mapping:\n   235→```\n   236→_session_map: dict[str, dict] = {}\n   237→# Key: Vista session_id\n   238→# Value: {\"provider\": \"claude\"|\"opencode\",\n   239→#         \"backend_session_id\": \"...\",\n   240→#         \"client\": ClaudeWSClient|OpenCodeClient}\n   241→```\n   242→\n   243→When a Vista session is created, the router creates a corresponding backend session.\n   244→When a Vista session is deleted, the router cleans up the backend session.\n   245→\n   246→### Changes to Existing Files\n   247→\n   248→| File | Change |\n   249→|------|--------|\n   250→| `server/services/chat_service.py` | **Rewrite**: Remove all subprocess logic. Delegate to `ProviderRouter`. Keep `build_prompt()` static method. |\n   251→| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Replace `_stream_response()` to use `ProviderRouter` instead of `chat_service.invoke_provider_streaming()`. Remove keepalive-manager integration (replaced by persistent WebSocket/SSE connections). |\n   252→| `server/routes/chat.py` | **Deprecate or remove**: The blocking `/api/projects/{project_id}/chat` endpoint is superseded by the session-based streaming flow. |\n   253→| `server/services/keepalive_manager.py` | **Remove or leave dormant**: The tmux-based keepalive approach is fully replaced by WebSocket (Claude) and REST+SSE (OpenCode) connections. |\n   254→\n   255→### Tests: `tests/test_provider_router.py`\n   256→\n   257→TDD candidate. Test routing logic, event translation for both providers, error handling, session lifecycle.\n   258→\n   259→---\n   260→\n   261→## Phase 3: Diagram Watcher Upgrade (Polling → watchdog)\n   262→\n   263→**Goal**: Replace 2s polling with instant filesystem event detection.\n   264→\n   265→### Changes to: `server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n   266→\n   267→Replace the `DiagramWatcher` class internals:\n   268→\n   269→```python\n   270→import watchdog.observers\n   271→import watchdog.events\n   272→\n   273→class DiagramEventHandler(watchdog.events.FileSystemEventHandler):\n   274→    \"\"\"Handles filesystem events for .mmd files.\"\"\"\n   275→\n   276→    def __init__(self, key: str, watcher: 'DiagramWatcher'):\n   277→        self.key = key\n   278→        self.watcher = watcher\n   279→\n   280→    def on_created(self, event):\n   281→        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n   282→            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_added\", event.src_path)\n   283→            self.watcher._update_manifest(self.key)\n   284→\n   285→    def on_modified(self, event):\n   286→        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n   287→            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_changed\", event.src_path)\n   288→\n   289→    def on_deleted(self, event):\n   290→        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n   291→            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_removed\", event.src_path)\n   292→            self.watcher._update_manifest(self.key)\n   293→\n   294→    def _is_diagram(self, path: str) -> bool:\n   295→        return Path(path).suffix in {\".mmd\", \".drawio\"}\n   296→```\n   297→\n   298→**Key changes**:\n   299→- Replace `_poll_loop()` with `watchdog.observers.Observer` per watched directory\n   300→- `subscribe()` creates an Observer if one doesn't exist for that key\n   301→- `unsubscribe()` stops the Observer when all subscribers leave\n   302→- Add debounce (100ms) to coalesce rapid file changes\n   303→- `_update_manifest()` reads the arch dir and regenerates `_arch.json`\n   304→\n   305→### Manifest Auto-Updater\n   306→\n   307→Within `DiagramWatcher._update_manifest()`:\n   308→- Scan arch dir for `.mmd` files\n   309→- For each file, read first few lines to detect `diagramType` (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n   310→- Generate `_arch.json` with name, file, type, diagramType fields\n   311→- Debounce to avoid rapid writes during bulk operations\n   312→\n   313→### Dependencies\n   314→\n   315→Add `watchdog` to `requirements.txt` / `pyproject.toml`.\n   316→\n   317→### Tests: `tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n   318→\n   319→TDD candidate. Test that create/edit/delete events fire correctly, manifest updates, debounce behavior.\n   320→\n   321→---\n   322→\n   323→## Phase 4: Context Assembler Refactor\n   324→\n   325→**Goal**: Preserve existing context assembly logic but extract it into a clean, testable module.\n   326→\n   327→### New File: `server/services/context_assembler.py`\n   328→\n   329→Extract from `chat_service.build_prompt()`:\n   330→\n   331→```python\n   332→class ContextAssembler:\n   333→    \"\"\"Assembles the full prompt from diagram context, history, and user message.\"\"\"\n   334→\n   335→    @staticmethod\n   336→    def build_system_prompt(arch_dir: str, specs_dir: str, project_root: str) -> str:\n   337→        \"\"\"Build the system prompt with scoped file access instructions.\"\"\"\n   338→        ...\n   339→\n   340→    @staticmethod\n   341→    def build_full_prompt(\n   342→        message: str,\n   343→        context: str | None,\n   344→        history: list[dict] | None,\n   345→        system_prompt: str,\n   346→    ) -> str:\n   347→        \"\"\"Assemble the complete prompt.\"\"\"\n   348→        ...\n   349→\n   350→    @staticmethod\n   351→    def get_diagram_context(\n   352→        arch_dir: str,\n   353→        attached_files: list[str],\n   354→        selected_elements: list[dict] | None = None,\n   355→    ) -> str:\n   356→        \"\"\"Read attached diagram files and format as context block.\"\"\"\n   357→        ...\n   358→```\n   359→\n   360→### Changes to Existing Files\n   361→\n   362→| File | Change |\n   363→|------|--------|\n   364→| `server/services/chat_service.py` | Replace `build_prompt()` with call to `ContextAssembler.build_full_prompt()` |\n   365→| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Import from `context_assembler` instead of `chat_service` |\n   366→\n   367→### Tests: `tests/test_context_assembler.py`\n   368→\n   369→TDD candidate. Test prompt assembly with various combinations of context/history/attachments.\n   370→\n   371→---\n   372→\n   373→## Phase 5: Model Discovery\n   374→\n   375→**Goal**: Dynamic model lists from both providers.\n   376→\n   377→### Changes to: `server/services/provider_service.py`\n   378→\n   379→Add methods to query models from running backend services:\n   380→\n   381→```python\n   382→class ClaudeProvider(Provider):\n   383→    def get_models(self) -> list[str]:\n   384→        # Keep static list: [\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]\n   385→        # Could enhance later via Companion's /api/backends/claude/models\n   386→        return [\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]\n   387→\n   388→class OpenCodeProvider(Provider):\n   389→    def get_models(self) -> list[str]:\n   390→        # Try querying running OpenCode server first\n   391→        try:\n   392→            # HTTP GET to http://localhost:{port}/config/providers\n   393→            # Parse response to extract model IDs\n   394→            ...\n   395→        except:\n   396→            # Fallback to CLI discovery\n   397→            return self._get_models_from_cli()\n   398→```\n   399→\n   400→### Changes to: `server/routes/providers.py`\n   401→\n   402→Ensure the existing `/api/providers` endpoint returns models from both providers.\n   403→\n   404→---\n   405→\n   406→## Phase 6: Frontend Changes\n   407→\n   408→**Goal**: Update `architecture.html` chat panel for WebSocket-based streaming.\n   409→\n   410→### Changes to: `server/views/architecture.html`\n   411→\n   412→The existing chat panel uses SSE (`EventSource`) for streaming. This pattern is preserved — Vista's SSE endpoint (`/api/projects/{id}/chat/sessions/{sid}/stream`) bridges to the backend WebSocket/SSE.\n   413→\n   414→**Frontend changes needed**:\n   415→\n   416→1. **Provider dropdown**: Add event handler that fetches models dynamically when provider changes via `GET /api/providers/{name}/models`\n   417→\n   418→2. **Service status indicators**: Add a status bar showing health of 3 services:\n   419→   ```html\n   420→   <div id=\"service-status\">\n   421→     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"vista\">Vista</span>\n   422→     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"companion\">Claude Bridge</span>\n   423→     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"opencode\">OpenCode</span>\n   424→   </div>\n   425→   ```\n   426→   Poll `GET /api/services/health` every 10s.\n   427→\n   428→3. **Provider availability**: Disable providers whose backend service is down. Gray out the dropdown option.\n   429→\n   430→4. **Toast notifications**: Show toast when a service goes down/recovers.\n   431→\n   432→5. **Diagram live updates**: The existing SSE handler for `diagram_changed`/`diagram_added`/`diagram_removed` events already re-renders Mermaid. No changes needed — only the backend watcher changes from polling to watchdog.\n   433→\n   434→6. **Session picker**: Already exists. No changes needed.\n   435→\n   436→---\n   437→\n   438→## Phase 7: Companion Fork Modifications\n   439→\n   440→**Goal**: Minimal changes to make Companion work as a backend-only service managed by Vista.\n   441→\n   442→### Changes needed in `vista/companion/`:\n   443→\n   444→1. **Port configuration**: Companion already reads `PORT` env var — Vista sets this when spawning.\n   445→\n   446→2. **Auto-approve mode**: When creating a session via `POST /api/sessions/create`, pass:\n   447→   ```json\n   448→   {\n   449→     \"model\": \"opus\",\n   450→     \"cwd\": \"/path/to/project\",\n   451→     \"permissionMode\": \"dangerously-skip-permissions\"\n   452→   }\n   453→   ```\n   454→   Companion's `CliLauncher.spawnCLI()` already handles `permissionMode` by passing it to Claude CLI.\n   455→\n   456→3. **Health endpoint**: Companion's `GET /api/sessions` serves as a health check (returns 200 when server is up). No changes needed.\n   457→\n   458→4. **CORS**: If Vista's FastAPI calls Companion APIs, ensure CORS is configured. Companion already has CORS middleware on `/api/*` routes. No changes needed since all calls are localhost.\n   459→\n   460→5. **No React frontend needed**: When `NODE_ENV=production`, Companion serves its built frontend. But since Vista never loads Companion's UI, this is harmless. **No changes needed**.\n   461→\n   462→### Summary: Zero or minimal changes to Companion fork\n   463→\n   464→The Companion fork is used as-is. Vista interacts through:\n   465→- `POST /api/sessions/create` — create session + spawn CLI\n   466→- `ws://.../ws/browser/{id}` — WebSocket for message exchange\n   467→- `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}` — cleanup\n   468→\n   469→---\n   470→\n   471→## Phase 8: Integration & Wiring\n   472→\n   473→### Updated `server/app.py` Lifespan\n   474→\n   475→```python\n   476→@asynccontextmanager\n   477→async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n   478→    config.ensure_full_path()\n   479→    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   480→    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n   481→\n   482→    # Start backend services\n   483→    await service_lifecycle.start_all()\n   484→\n   485→    yield\n   486→\n   487→    # Shutdown\n   488→    await service_lifecycle.stop_all()\n   489→    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n   490→    await provider_router.cleanup()\n   491→```\n   492→\n   493→### Updated `server/routes/chat_sessions.py`\n   494→\n   495→The `_stream_response()` function changes from subprocess-based to router-based:\n   496→\n   497→```python\n   498→async def _stream_response(project_id, session_id, provider, model, prompt, project_path):\n   499→    full_text = []\n   500→    try:\n   501→        async for event in provider_router.send_message(\n   502→            provider=provider,\n   503→            model=model,\n   504→            prompt=prompt,\n   505→            session_id=session_id,\n   506→            cwd=project_path,\n   507→        ):\n   508→            if event[\"type\"] == \"token\":\n   509→                full_text.append(event[\"text\"])\n   510→                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"token\", \"data\": {\"text\": event[\"text\"]}})\n   511→            elif event[\"type\"] == \"done\":\n   512→                content = event.get(\"content\", \"\".join(full_text))\n   513→                ChatSessionService.add_message(project_id, session_id, \"assistant\", content)\n   514→                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"message_done\", \"data\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}})\n   515→            elif event[\"type\"] == \"error\":\n   516→                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"chat_error\", \"data\": {\"detail\": event[\"detail\"]}})\n   517→    except Exception as e:\n   518→        await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"chat_error\", \"data\": {\"detail\": str(e)}})\n   519→```\n   520→\n   521→---\n   522→\n   523→## Dependency Summary\n   524→\n   525→### New Python packages\n   526→\n   527→| Package | Purpose |\n   528→|---------|---------|\n   529→| `watchdog` | Filesystem event monitoring (replaces polling) |\n   530→| `websockets` | Async WebSocket client for Companion bridge |\n   531→| `httpx` | Async HTTP client for OpenCode REST API |\n   532→| `httpx-sse` | SSE parsing for OpenCode streaming |\n   533→\n   534→### New system dependencies\n   535→\n   536→| Dependency | Purpose | Required? |\n   537→|------------|---------|-----------|\n   538→| `bun` | Companion server runtime | For Claude provider |\n   539→| `claude` CLI | Claude Code | For Claude provider |\n   540→| `opencode` binary | OpenCode server | For OpenCode provider |\n   541→\n   542→All are optional — graceful degradation when not installed.\n   543→\n   544→---\n   545→\n   546→## Implementation Order\n   547→\n   548→| Step | Phase | Files | Dependencies |\n   549→|------|-------|-------|-------------|\n   550→| 1 | Phase 1 | `service_lifecycle.py`, `routes/service_status.py` | None |\n   551→| 2 | Phase 1 | `app.py` lifespan changes | Step 1 |\n   552→| 3 | Phase 3 | `diagram_watcher.py` rewrite | watchdog package |\n   553→| 4 | Phase 4 | `context_assembler.py` | None |\n   554→| 5 | Phase 2 | `claude_ws_client.py` | websockets package, Step 1 (Companion running) |\n   555→| 6 | Phase 2 | `opencode_client.py` | httpx/httpx-sse packages, Step 1 (OpenCode running) |\n   556→| 7 | Phase 2 | `provider_router.py` | Steps 5+6 |\n   557→| 8 | Phase 2 | `chat_service.py` rewrite, `chat_sessions.py` update | Steps 4+7 |\n   558→| 9 | Phase 5 | `provider_service.py` model discovery | Steps 1+6 |\n   559→| 10 | Phase 6 | `architecture.html` frontend changes | Steps 1+8 |\n   560→| 11 | Phase 7 | Companion fork verification | Step 1 |\n   561→| 12 | Phase 8 | Final integration, wiring, cleanup | All above |\n   562→\n   563→---\n   564→\n   565→## Files Summary\n   566→\n   567→### New Files\n   568→\n   569→| File | Purpose |\n   570→|------|---------|\n   571→| `server/services/service_lifecycle.py` | Multi-service lifecycle management |\n   572→| `server/services/provider_router.py` | Route messages to Claude/OpenCode backends |\n   573→| `server/services/claude_ws_client.py` | WebSocket client for Companion bridge |\n   574→| `server/services/opencode_client.py` | HTTP+SSE client for OpenCode server |\n   575→| `server/services/context_assembler.py` | Prompt assembly (extracted from chat_service) |\n   576→| `server/routes/service_status.py` | Health status API endpoint |\n   577→| `tests/test_service_lifecycle.py` | Lifecycle manager tests |\n   578→| `tests/test_provider_router.py` | Provider routing tests |\n   579→| `tests/test_context_assembler.py` | Context assembly tests |\n   580→| `tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Watchdog-based watcher tests |\n   581→\n   582→### Modified Files\n   583→\n   584→| File | Change Summary |\n   585→|------|---------------|\n   586→| `server/app.py` | Lifecycle integration in lifespan, new route import |\n   587→| `server/config.py` | Add `get_chat_settings()` for companion/opencode config |\n   588→| `server/services/chat_service.py` | Remove subprocess logic, delegate to ProviderRouter |\n   589→| `server/services/chat_session_service.py` | No changes needed |\n   590→| `server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Rewrite from polling to watchdog |\n   591→| `server/services/provider_service.py` | Add live model discovery from running services |\n   592→| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Use ProviderRouter, remove keepalive integration |\n   593→| `server/routes/architecture.py` | No changes needed |\n   594→| `server/views/architecture.html` | Service status bar, provider availability, toasts |\n   595→| `mcp_server.py` | Delegate OpenCode management to lifecycle manager |\n   596→| `server/models/chat_session.py` | No changes needed |\n   597→\n   598→### Removed/Deprecated Files\n   599→\n   600→| File | Reason |\n   601→|------|--------|\n   602→| `server/services/keepalive_manager.py` | Replaced by WebSocket/SSE connections |\n   603→| `server/routes/chat.py` | Blocking endpoint superseded by streaming sessions |\n   604→\n   605→### Unchanged Companion Files\n   606→\n   607→The `vista/companion/` directory requires **zero changes**. Vista interacts via:\n   608→- HTTP REST: `POST /api/sessions/create`, `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}`\n   609→- WebSocket: `ws://localhost:{port}/ws/browser/{session_id}`\n   610→\n   611→---\n   612→\n   613→## Risk Assessment\n   614→\n   615→| Risk | Mitigation |\n   616→|------|-----------|\n   617→| Companion's Bun runtime not installed | Detect at startup, disable Claude provider, show in service status |\n   618→| OpenCode binary not installed | Detect at startup, disable OpenCode provider, show in service status |\n   619→| WebSocket connection drops | Auto-reconnect with exponential backoff in `claude_ws_client.py` |\n   620→| OpenCode SSE stream disconnects | Re-subscribe on disconnect, handle partial events |\n   621→| watchdog missing platform support | watchdog has a polling fallback; Windows is well-supported |\n   622→| Port conflicts | Use `_find_free_port()` pattern already in codebase |\n   623→| Companion process crash mid-chat | Lifecycle manager auto-restarts; ProviderRouter surfaces error to frontend |\n   624→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"615fcba1-13a5-40a3-839d-703775331047","uuid":"db834f05-87ee-4a49-bda5-4d0ae303b25e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Architecture Chat\n\n## Overview\n\nReplace the subprocess-based CLI chat with two first-class provider backends:\n1. **Claude** via Companion fork's WebSocket bridge (`vista/companion/`)\n2. **OpenCode** via `opencode serve` HTTP REST + SSE streaming\n\nVista's FastAPI server remains the single hub. The existing Jinja2/vanilla JS frontend is kept; Companion's React UI is NOT used.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Service Lifecycle Manager\n\n**Goal**: Auto-start/stop/restart Companion and OpenCode alongside the Vista FastAPI server.\n\n### New File: `server/services/service_lifecycle.py`\n\nA `ServiceLifecycleManager` class managing named service instances:\n\n```\nServiceInstance:\n  name: str              # \"companion\" | \"opencode\"\n  command: list[str]     # e.g. [\"bun\", \"web/server/index.ts\"]\n  cwd: str               # working directory\n  port: int              # assigned port\n  health_url: str        # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/sessions\"\n  status: str            # stopped | starting | running | error | restarting\n  pid: int | None\n  process: Popen | None\n  started_at: float | None\n  restart_count: int\n  max_restarts: int      # default 5\n  backoff_seconds: float  # exponential: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (capped)\n```\n\n**State machine** (matches `state-service-lifecycle.mmd`):\n- `Stopped -> Starting -> Running -> Stopping -> Stopped`\n- `Running -> Error -> Restarting -> Starting`\n- `Error -> Stopped` (max retries exceeded)\n\n**Methods**:\n- `start(name)` — spawn process, wait for health\n- `stop(name)` — graceful terminate, force kill after 5s\n- `restart(name)` — stop then start\n- `health_check(name)` — HTTP GET to health_url\n- `start_all()` — called from `app_lifespan` or `mcp_server.app_lifespan`\n- `stop_all()` — called on shutdown\n- `get_status(name)` — return ServiceInstance snapshot\n- `get_all_status()` — return all services\n\n**Periodic health checker**: asyncio task, every 10s, 3 consecutive failures triggers restart with backoff.\n\n**Integration points**:\n- `server/app.py` lifespan: call `lifecycle.start_all()` on startup, `lifecycle.stop_all()` on shutdown\n- `mcp_server.py` lifespan: also calls `lifecycle.start_all()` so services start regardless of entry point\n\n### Companion Service Config\n\n```python\nServiceConfig(\n    name=\"companion\",\n    command=[\"bun\", \"web/server/index.ts\"],\n    cwd=str(PLUGIN_ROOT / \"companion\" / \"web\"),\n    preferred_port=3457,\n    health_url=\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/api/sessions\",\n    env={\"NODE_ENV\": \"production\", \"PORT\": \"{port}\"},\n)\n```\n\n**Prerequisites check**: `shutil.which(\"bun\")` — if not found, skip Companion startup and disable Claude provider.\n\n### OpenCode Service Config\n\n```python\nServiceConfig(\n    name=\"opencode\",\n    command=[\"opencode\", \"serve\", \"--port\", \"{port}\"],\n    preferred_port=4096,\n    health_url=\"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/global/health\",\n)\n```\n\n**Prerequisites check**: `shutil.which(\"opencode\")` — if not found, skip OpenCode startup and disable OpenCode provider.\n\n### Changes to Existing Files\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | Import lifecycle manager, call `start_all()`/`stop_all()` in lifespan |\n| `server/config.py` | Add `get_chat_settings()` returning companion/opencode port config |\n| `mcp_server.py` | Remove inline `_start_opencode_serve()`, delegate to lifecycle manager |\n\n### New Route: `server/routes/service_status.py`\n\n```\nGET /api/services/health → {services: [{name, port, status, uptime, pid}]}\n```\n\n### Tests: `tests/test_service_lifecycle.py`\n\nTDD candidate. Test state transitions, backoff calculation, max retry cap.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Provider Router (Claude WebSocket + OpenCode SSE)\n\n**Goal**: Replace the subprocess-based `ChatService` with protocol-native provider backends.\n\n### New File: `server/services/provider_router.py`\n\n```python\nclass ProviderRouter:\n    \"\"\"Routes chat messages to the correct backend based on provider type.\"\"\"\n\n    async def send_message(\n        self,\n        provider: str,       # \"claude\" | \"opencode\"\n        model: str,\n        prompt: str,          # fully assembled prompt\n        session_id: str,      # Vista's session ID\n        cwd: str,             # project root for Claude CLI\n    ) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n        \"\"\"Yield streaming events: {type: \"token\"|\"done\"|\"error\", ...}\"\"\"\n        if provider == \"claude\":\n            async for event in self._send_claude(model, prompt, session_id, cwd):\n                yield event\n        elif provider == \"opencode\":\n            async for event in self._send_opencode(model, prompt, session_id):\n                yield event\n        else:\n            yield {\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": f\"Unknown provider: {provider}\"}\n```\n\n### Claude Provider: WebSocket Bridge to Companion\n\n**New File**: `server/services/claude_ws_client.py`\n\n```python\nclass ClaudeWSClient:\n    \"\"\"WebSocket client connecting to Companion's /ws/browser/{session_id} endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, companion_url: str):\n        self.companion_url = companion_url  # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:3457\"\n        self._ws = None\n        self._session_id = None\n\n    async def create_session(self, model: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"POST /api/sessions/create → returns Companion session ID.\n\n        Companion spawns Claude CLI with --sdk-url, --dangerously-skip-permissions,\n        --model, --verbose, --output-format stream-json.\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def connect(self, session_id: str):\n        \"\"\"Connect to ws://{companion_url}/ws/browser/{session_id}\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def send_message(self, text: str) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n        \"\"\"Send user message and yield streaming events.\n\n        Send: {\"type\": \"user\", \"message\": {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": text}}\n\n        Receive and translate:\n        - {\"type\": \"stream_event\", \"event\": {\"type\": \"content_block_delta\",\n           \"delta\": {\"text\": \"tok\"}}} → {\"type\": \"token\", \"text\": \"tok\"}\n        - {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": ...} → {\"type\": \"done\", \"content\": \"...\"}\n        - {\"type\": \"result\", ...} → {\"type\": \"result\", ...}\n        - {\"type\": \"permission_request\", ...} → auto-approve immediately\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def disconnect(self):\n        \"\"\"Close WebSocket connection.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def delete_session(self, session_id: str):\n        \"\"\"DELETE /api/sessions/{session_id}\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\nUses `websockets` library (async WebSocket client for Python). Add to dependencies.\n\n**Permission auto-approve**: If a `permission_request` arrives (shouldn't normally with `--dangerously-skip-permissions`), respond with:\n```json\n{\"type\": \"permission_response\", \"request_id\": \"...\", \"behavior\": \"allow\", \"updated_input\": {...}}\n```\n\n### OpenCode Provider: HTTP REST + SSE\n\n**New File**: `server/services/opencode_client.py`\n\n```python\nclass OpenCodeClient:\n    \"\"\"Async client for OpenCode's REST API + SSE streaming.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base_url: str):\n        self.base_url = base_url  # e.g. \"http://127.0.0.1:4096\"\n\n    async def create_session(self, title: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"POST /session → returns session ID\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def send_message_streaming(\n        self, session_id: str, text: str, model: dict | None = None\n    ) -> AsyncGenerator[dict, None]:\n        \"\"\"POST /session/{id}/prompt_async, then subscribe to GET /event SSE.\n\n        Translate events:\n        - event: message.part.updated → {\"type\": \"token\", \"text\": delta}\n        - event: session.idle → {\"type\": \"done\", \"content\": full_text}\n        - event: session.error → {\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": msg}\n        \"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def get_providers(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"GET /config/providers → provider/model list for model selection\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def delete_session(self, session_id: str):\n        \"\"\"DELETE /session/{id}\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    async def abort_session(self, session_id: str):\n        \"\"\"POST /session/{id}/abort\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\nUses `httpx` for async HTTP and SSE (via `httpx-sse`). Add to dependencies.\n\n### Session Mapping\n\nThe ProviderRouter maintains a mapping:\n```\n_session_map: dict[str, dict] = {}\n# Key: Vista session_id\n# Value: {\"provider\": \"claude\"|\"opencode\",\n#         \"backend_session_id\": \"...\",\n#         \"client\": ClaudeWSClient|OpenCodeClient}\n```\n\nWhen a Vista session is created, the router creates a corresponding backend session.\nWhen a Vista session is deleted, the router cleans up the backend session.\n\n### Changes to Existing Files\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/services/chat_service.py` | **Rewrite**: Remove all subprocess logic. Delegate to `ProviderRouter`. Keep `build_prompt()` static method. |\n| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Replace `_stream_response()` to use `ProviderRouter` instead of `chat_service.invoke_provider_streaming()`. Remove keepalive-manager integration (replaced by persistent WebSocket/SSE connections). |\n| `server/routes/chat.py` | **Deprecate or remove**: The blocking `/api/projects/{project_id}/chat` endpoint is superseded by the session-based streaming flow. |\n| `server/services/keepalive_manager.py` | **Remove or leave dormant**: The tmux-based keepalive approach is fully replaced by WebSocket (Claude) and REST+SSE (OpenCode) connections. |\n\n### Tests: `tests/test_provider_router.py`\n\nTDD candidate. Test routing logic, event translation for both providers, error handling, session lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Diagram Watcher Upgrade (Polling → watchdog)\n\n**Goal**: Replace 2s polling with instant filesystem event detection.\n\n### Changes to: `server/services/diagram_watcher.py`\n\nReplace the `DiagramWatcher` class internals:\n\n```python\nimport watchdog.observers\nimport watchdog.events\n\nclass DiagramEventHandler(watchdog.events.FileSystemEventHandler):\n    \"\"\"Handles filesystem events for .mmd files.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, key: str, watcher: 'DiagramWatcher'):\n        self.key = key\n        self.watcher = watcher\n\n    def on_created(self, event):\n        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_added\", event.src_path)\n            self.watcher._update_manifest(self.key)\n\n    def on_modified(self, event):\n        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_changed\", event.src_path)\n\n    def on_deleted(self, event):\n        if self._is_diagram(event.src_path):\n            self.watcher._enqueue_event(self.key, \"diagram_removed\", event.src_path)\n            self.watcher._update_manifest(self.key)\n\n    def _is_diagram(self, path: str) -> bool:\n        return Path(path).suffix in {\".mmd\", \".drawio\"}\n```\n\n**Key changes**:\n- Replace `_poll_loop()` with `watchdog.observers.Observer` per watched directory\n- `subscribe()` creates an Observer if one doesn't exist for that key\n- `unsubscribe()` stops the Observer when all subscribers leave\n- Add debounce (100ms) to coalesce rapid file changes\n- `_update_manifest()` reads the arch dir and regenerates `_arch.json`\n\n### Manifest Auto-Updater\n\nWithin `DiagramWatcher._update_manifest()`:\n- Scan arch dir for `.mmd` files\n- For each file, read first few lines to detect `diagramType` (flowchart, sequence, etc.)\n- Generate `_arch.json` with name, file, type, diagramType fields\n- Debounce to avoid rapid writes during bulk operations\n\n### Dependencies\n\nAdd `watchdog` to `requirements.txt` / `pyproject.toml`.\n\n### Tests: `tests/test_diagram_watcher.py`\n\nTDD candidate. Test that create/edit/delete events fire correctly, manifest updates, debounce behavior.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Context Assembler Refactor\n\n**Goal**: Preserve existing context assembly logic but extract it into a clean, testable module.\n\n### New File: `server/services/context_assembler.py`\n\nExtract from `chat_service.build_prompt()`:\n\n```python\nclass ContextAssembler:\n    \"\"\"Assembles the full prompt from diagram context, history, and user message.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def build_system_prompt(arch_dir: str, specs_dir: str, project_root: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Build the system prompt with scoped file access instructions.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def build_full_prompt(\n        message: str,\n        context: str | None,\n        history: list[dict] | None,\n        system_prompt: str,\n    ) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Assemble the complete prompt.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def get_diagram_context(\n        arch_dir: str,\n        attached_files: list[str],\n        selected_elements: list[dict] | None = None,\n    ) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Read attached diagram files and format as context block.\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\n### Changes to Existing Files\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/services/chat_service.py` | Replace `build_prompt()` with call to `ContextAssembler.build_full_prompt()` |\n| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Import from `context_assembler` instead of `chat_service` |\n\n### Tests: `tests/test_context_assembler.py`\n\nTDD candidate. Test prompt assembly with various combinations of context/history/attachments.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Model Discovery\n\n**Goal**: Dynamic model lists from both providers.\n\n### Changes to: `server/services/provider_service.py`\n\nAdd methods to query models from running backend services:\n\n```python\nclass ClaudeProvider(Provider):\n    def get_models(self) -> list[str]:\n        # Keep static list: [\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]\n        # Could enhance later via Companion's /api/backends/claude/models\n        return [\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]\n\nclass OpenCodeProvider(Provider):\n    def get_models(self) -> list[str]:\n        # Try querying running OpenCode server first\n        try:\n            # HTTP GET to http://localhost:{port}/config/providers\n            # Parse response to extract model IDs\n            ...\n        except:\n            # Fallback to CLI discovery\n            return self._get_models_from_cli()\n```\n\n### Changes to: `server/routes/providers.py`\n\nEnsure the existing `/api/providers` endpoint returns models from both providers.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Frontend Changes\n\n**Goal**: Update `architecture.html` chat panel for WebSocket-based streaming.\n\n### Changes to: `server/views/architecture.html`\n\nThe existing chat panel uses SSE (`EventSource`) for streaming. This pattern is preserved — Vista's SSE endpoint (`/api/projects/{id}/chat/sessions/{sid}/stream`) bridges to the backend WebSocket/SSE.\n\n**Frontend changes needed**:\n\n1. **Provider dropdown**: Add event handler that fetches models dynamically when provider changes via `GET /api/providers/{name}/models`\n\n2. **Service status indicators**: Add a status bar showing health of 3 services:\n   ```html\n   <div id=\"service-status\">\n     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"vista\">Vista</span>\n     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"companion\">Claude Bridge</span>\n     <span class=\"service-dot\" data-service=\"opencode\">OpenCode</span>\n   </div>\n   ```\n   Poll `GET /api/services/health` every 10s.\n\n3. **Provider availability**: Disable providers whose backend service is down. Gray out the dropdown option.\n\n4. **Toast notifications**: Show toast when a service goes down/recovers.\n\n5. **Diagram live updates**: The existing SSE handler for `diagram_changed`/`diagram_added`/`diagram_removed` events already re-renders Mermaid. No changes needed — only the backend watcher changes from polling to watchdog.\n\n6. **Session picker**: Already exists. No changes needed.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Companion Fork Modifications\n\n**Goal**: Minimal changes to make Companion work as a backend-only service managed by Vista.\n\n### Changes needed in `vista/companion/`:\n\n1. **Port configuration**: Companion already reads `PORT` env var — Vista sets this when spawning.\n\n2. **Auto-approve mode**: When creating a session via `POST /api/sessions/create`, pass:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"model\": \"opus\",\n     \"cwd\": \"/path/to/project\",\n     \"permissionMode\": \"dangerously-skip-permissions\"\n   }\n   ```\n   Companion's `CliLauncher.spawnCLI()` already handles `permissionMode` by passing it to Claude CLI.\n\n3. **Health endpoint**: Companion's `GET /api/sessions` serves as a health check (returns 200 when server is up). No changes needed.\n\n4. **CORS**: If Vista's FastAPI calls Companion APIs, ensure CORS is configured. Companion already has CORS middleware on `/api/*` routes. No changes needed since all calls are localhost.\n\n5. **No React frontend needed**: When `NODE_ENV=production`, Companion serves its built frontend. But since Vista never loads Companion's UI, this is harmless. **No changes needed**.\n\n### Summary: Zero or minimal changes to Companion fork\n\nThe Companion fork is used as-is. Vista interacts through:\n- `POST /api/sessions/create` — create session + spawn CLI\n- `ws://.../ws/browser/{id}` — WebSocket for message exchange\n- `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}` — cleanup\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Integration & Wiring\n\n### Updated `server/app.py` Lifespan\n\n```python\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    config.ensure_full_path()\n    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Start backend services\n    await service_lifecycle.start_all()\n\n    yield\n\n    # Shutdown\n    await service_lifecycle.stop_all()\n    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n    await provider_router.cleanup()\n```\n\n### Updated `server/routes/chat_sessions.py`\n\nThe `_stream_response()` function changes from subprocess-based to router-based:\n\n```python\nasync def _stream_response(project_id, session_id, provider, model, prompt, project_path):\n    full_text = []\n    try:\n        async for event in provider_router.send_message(\n            provider=provider,\n            model=model,\n            prompt=prompt,\n            session_id=session_id,\n            cwd=project_path,\n        ):\n            if event[\"type\"] == \"token\":\n                full_text.append(event[\"text\"])\n                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"token\", \"data\": {\"text\": event[\"text\"]}})\n            elif event[\"type\"] == \"done\":\n                content = event.get(\"content\", \"\".join(full_text))\n                ChatSessionService.add_message(project_id, session_id, \"assistant\", content)\n                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"message_done\", \"data\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}})\n            elif event[\"type\"] == \"error\":\n                await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"chat_error\", \"data\": {\"detail\": event[\"detail\"]}})\n    except Exception as e:\n        await _broadcast(session_id, {\"event\": \"chat_error\", \"data\": {\"detail\": str(e)}})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependency Summary\n\n### New Python packages\n\n| Package | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `watchdog` | Filesystem event monitoring (replaces polling) |\n| `websockets` | Async WebSocket client for Companion bridge |\n| `httpx` | Async HTTP client for OpenCode REST API |\n| `httpx-sse` | SSE parsing for OpenCode streaming |\n\n### New system dependencies\n\n| Dependency | Purpose | Required? |\n|------------|---------|-----------|\n| `bun` | Companion server runtime | For Claude provider |\n| `claude` CLI | Claude Code | For Claude provider |\n| `opencode` binary | OpenCode server | For OpenCode provider |\n\nAll are optional — graceful degradation when not installed.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n| Step | Phase | Files | Dependencies |\n|------|-------|-------|-------------|\n| 1 | Phase 1 | `service_lifecycle.py`, `routes/service_status.py` | None |\n| 2 | Phase 1 | `app.py` lifespan changes | Step 1 |\n| 3 | Phase 3 | `diagram_watcher.py` rewrite | watchdog package |\n| 4 | Phase 4 | `context_assembler.py` | None |\n| 5 | Phase 2 | `claude_ws_client.py` | websockets package, Step 1 (Companion running) |\n| 6 | Phase 2 | `opencode_client.py` | httpx/httpx-sse packages, Step 1 (OpenCode running) |\n| 7 | Phase 2 | `provider_router.py` | Steps 5+6 |\n| 8 | Phase 2 | `chat_service.py` rewrite, `chat_sessions.py` update | Steps 4+7 |\n| 9 | Phase 5 | `provider_service.py` model discovery | Steps 1+6 |\n| 10 | Phase 6 | `architecture.html` frontend changes | Steps 1+8 |\n| 11 | Phase 7 | Companion fork verification | Step 1 |\n| 12 | Phase 8 | Final integration, wiring, cleanup | All above |\n\n---\n\n## Files Summary\n\n### New Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `server/services/service_lifecycle.py` | Multi-service lifecycle management |\n| `server/services/provider_router.py` | Route messages to Claude/OpenCode backends |\n| `server/services/claude_ws_client.py` | WebSocket client for Companion bridge |\n| `server/services/opencode_client.py` | HTTP+SSE client for OpenCode server |\n| `server/services/context_assembler.py` | Prompt assembly (extracted from chat_service) |\n| `server/routes/service_status.py` | Health status API endpoint |\n| `tests/test_service_lifecycle.py` | Lifecycle manager tests |\n| `tests/test_provider_router.py` | Provider routing tests |\n| `tests/test_context_assembler.py` | Context assembly tests |\n| `tests/test_diagram_watcher.py` | Watchdog-based watcher tests |\n\n### Modified Files\n\n| File | Change Summary |\n|------|---------------|\n| `server/app.py` | Lifecycle integration in lifespan, new route import |\n| `server/config.py` | Add `get_chat_settings()` for companion/opencode config |\n| `server/services/chat_service.py` | Remove subprocess logic, delegate to ProviderRouter |\n| `server/services/chat_session_service.py` | No changes needed |\n| `server/services/diagram_watcher.py` | Rewrite from polling to watchdog |\n| `server/services/provider_service.py` | Add live model discovery from running services |\n| `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` | Use ProviderRouter, remove keepalive integration |\n| `server/routes/architecture.py` | No changes needed |\n| `server/views/architecture.html` | Service status bar, provider availability, toasts |\n| `mcp_server.py` | Delegate OpenCode management to lifecycle manager |\n| `server/models/chat_session.py` | No changes needed |\n\n### Removed/Deprecated Files\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/services/keepalive_manager.py` | Replaced by WebSocket/SSE connections |\n| `server/routes/chat.py` | Blocking endpoint superseded by streaming sessions |\n\n### Unchanged Companion Files\n\nThe `vista/companion/` directory requires **zero changes**. Vista interacts via:\n- HTTP REST: `POST /api/sessions/create`, `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}`\n- WebSocket: `ws://localhost:{port}/ws/browser/{session_id}`\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|\n| Companion's Bun runtime not installed | Detect at startup, disable Claude provider, show in service status |\n| OpenCode binary not installed | Detect at startup, disable OpenCode provider, show in service status |\n| WebSocket connection drops | Auto-reconnect with exponential backoff in `claude_ws_client.py` |\n| OpenCode SSE stream disconnects | Re-subscribe on disconnect, handle partial events |\n| watchdog missing platform support | watchdog has a polling fallback; Windows is well-supported |\n| Port conflicts | Use `_find_free_port()` pattern already in codebase |\n| Companion process crash mid-chat | Lifecycle manager auto-restarts; ProviderRouter surfaces error to frontend |\n","numLines":624,"startLine":1,"totalLines":624}}}
