{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TMNJY9uR8rV5HvbfumpDYr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# OpenCode Server API Reference\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→OpenCode provides a headless HTTP server mode (`opencode serve`) that exposes a REST API with SSE streaming for real-time events. This is the integration point for Vista's OpenCode provider.\n     6→\n     7→## Starting the Server\n     8→\n     9→```bash\n    10→opencode serve [--port <number>] [--hostname <string>] [--cors <origin>]\n    11→```\n    12→\n    13→| Flag | Default | Description |\n    14→|------|---------|-------------|\n    15→| `--port` | 4096 | HTTP port |\n    16→| `--hostname` | 127.0.0.1 | Bind address |\n    17→| `--cors` | none | CORS origin (repeatable) |\n    18→\n    19→**Authentication** (optional):\n    20→```bash\n    21→OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=secret opencode serve\n    22→OPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME=custom-user  # default: \"opencode\"\n    23→```\n    24→When set, all endpoints require HTTP Basic Auth: `Authorization: Basic <base64(user:pass)>`\n    25→\n    26→## Core Endpoints\n    27→\n    28→### Health\n    29→```\n    30→GET /global/health → {status, version}\n    31→```\n    32→\n    33→### Sessions\n    34→\n    35→**Create session:**\n    36→```\n    37→POST /session\n    38→Content-Type: application/json\n    39→\n    40→{\n    41→  \"title\": \"Architecture Chat - docker-sandbox\",\n    42→  \"permission\": [\"read\", \"write\"]\n    43→}\n    44→→ {id, title, ...}\n    45→```\n    46→\n    47→**List sessions:**\n    48→```\n    49→GET /session → [{id, title, ...}]\n    50→```\n    51→\n    52→**Get session:**\n    53→```\n    54→GET /session/:id → {id, title, messages, ...}\n    55→```\n    56→\n    57→**Delete session:**\n    58→```\n    59→DELETE /session/:id\n    60→```\n    61→\n    62→### Messages\n    63→\n    64→**Send message (blocking):**\n    65→```\n    66→POST /session/:id/message\n    67→Content-Type: application/json\n    68→\n    69→{\n    70→  \"parts\": [\n    71→    {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Your message here\"}\n    72→  ],\n    73→  \"model\": {\n    74→    \"providerID\": \"anthropic\",\n    75→    \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"\n    76→  }\n    77→}\n    78→→ {info, parts}\n    79→```\n    80→\n    81→**Send message (async, non-blocking):**\n    82→```\n    83→POST /session/:id/prompt_async\n    84→Content-Type: application/json\n    85→\n    86→{\n    87→  \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"...\"}],\n    88→  \"model\": {\"providerID\": \"anthropic\", \"modelID\": \"...\"}\n    89→}\n    90→```\n    91→\n    92→**Abort running session:**\n    93→```\n    94→POST /session/:id/abort\n    95→```\n    96→\n    97→**List messages:**\n    98→```\n    99→GET /session/:id/message → [{id, role, parts, ...}]\n   100→```\n   101→\n   102→### Streaming (SSE)\n   103→\n   104→**Global event stream:**\n   105→```\n   106→GET /global/event\n   107→Accept: text/event-stream\n   108→```\n   109→\n   110→**Session-scoped event stream:**\n   111→```\n   112→GET /event\n   113→Accept: text/event-stream\n   114→```\n   115→\n   116→**Event format:**\n   117→```\n   118→event: message.part.updated\n   119→data: {\"type\":\"message.part.updated\",\"properties\":{...}}\n   120→```\n   121→\n   122→### Event Types\n   123→\n   124→| Event | Description |\n   125→|-------|-------------|\n   126→| `server.connected` | Sent immediately on SSE connect |\n   127→| `session.created` | New session created |\n   128→| `session.updated` | Session metadata changed |\n   129→| `session.deleted` | Session removed |\n   130→| `session.idle` | Session finished processing (response complete) |\n   131→| `session.error` | Session encountered error |\n   132→| `message.updated` | Message metadata changed |\n   133→| `message.part.updated` | **Streaming text delta** — incremental token updates |\n   134→| `message.part.removed` | Message part deleted |\n   135→| `message.deleted` | Full message removed |\n   136→| `permission.asked` | Tool permission request |\n   137→| `permission.response` | Tool permission response |\n   138→| `file.changed` | File modified on disk |\n   139→| `file.watcher.updated` | File watcher state change |\n   140→| `lsp.diagnostics` | LSP diagnostic update |\n   141→\n   142→**Key for streaming:** `message.part.updated` events contain incremental text deltas that should be appended to the current message to display real-time token streaming.\n   143→\n   144→### Configuration\n   145→\n   146→**Get config:**\n   147→```\n   148→GET /config → {providers, models, ...}\n   149→```\n   150→\n   151→**Get available providers/models:**\n   152→```\n   153→GET /config/providers → [{id, models: [...]}]\n   154→```\n   155→\n   156→### Model Selection\n   157→\n   158→Models are specified per-message, not per-session:\n   159→```json\n   160→{\n   161→  \"model\": {\n   162→    \"providerID\": \"anthropic\",\n   163→    \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"\n   164→  }\n   165→}\n   166→```\n   167→\n   168→Common provider IDs: `anthropic`, `openai`, `google`, `ollama`\n   169→\n   170→**Note:** There are known issues where per-message model selection may be ignored in favor of server defaults (GitHub issue #3517). Test thoroughly.\n   171→\n   172→## Python SDK\n   173→\n   174→```bash\n   175→pip install --pre opencode-ai\n   176→```\n   177→\n   178→### Synchronous Usage\n   179→```python\n   180→from opencode_ai import Opencode\n   181→\n   182→client = Opencode(base_url=\"http://localhost:4096\")\n   183→\n   184→# List sessions\n   185→sessions = client.session.list()\n   186→\n   187→# Create session\n   188→session = client.session.create(title=\"Arch Chat\", permission=[\"read\", \"write\"])\n   189→\n   190→# Send message\n   191→response = client.session.prompt(\n   192→    id=session.id,\n   193→    parts=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello\"}],\n   194→    model={\"providerID\": \"anthropic\", \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"}\n   195→)\n   196→\n   197→# Stream events\n   198→stream = client.event.list()\n   199→for events in stream:\n   200→    for event in events:\n   201→        if event.type == \"message.part.updated\":\n   202→            print(event.properties.text, end=\"\", flush=True)\n   203→```\n   204→\n   205→### Async Usage\n   206→```python\n   207→from opencode_ai import AsyncOpencode\n   208→\n   209→client = AsyncOpencode(base_url=\"http://localhost:4096\")\n   210→sessions = await client.session.list()\n   211→```\n   212→\n   213→## Integration Notes for Vista\n   214→\n   215→### Session Mapping\n   216→Vista maintains a mapping between its own `ChatSession.id` and OpenCode's session IDs. When creating a Vista chat session with provider \"opencode\", Vista also creates an OpenCode session and stores the mapping.\n   217→\n   218→### Context Assembly\n   219→Vista assembles the full prompt (system instructions + diagram context + history + user message) into a single text part before sending to OpenCode. OpenCode does not know about Vista's context structure.\n   220→\n   221→### Streaming Bridge\n   222→Vista subscribes to OpenCode's SSE `GET /event` endpoint and translates `message.part.updated` events into Vista's own SSE format (`event: token`) for the browser frontend.\n   223→\n   224→### Health Checking\n   225→Use `GET /global/health` for service health monitoring. Expected response includes server status and version info.\n   226→\n   227→### Lifecycle Management\n   228→Vista starts OpenCode via:\n   229→```python\n   230→proc = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(\n   231→    \"opencode\", \"serve\", \"--port\", str(port),\n   232→    stdout=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,\n   233→    stderr=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE\n   234→)\n   235→```\n   236→Monitor process health with periodic `GET /global/health` checks.\n   237→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"615fcba1-13a5-40a3-839d-703775331047","uuid":"fa0da87e-f9f1-42a7-b3e3-7d0d02b1227e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/opencode-server-reference.md","content":"# OpenCode Server API Reference\n\n## Overview\n\nOpenCode provides a headless HTTP server mode (`opencode serve`) that exposes a REST API with SSE streaming for real-time events. This is the integration point for Vista's OpenCode provider.\n\n## Starting the Server\n\n```bash\nopencode serve [--port <number>] [--hostname <string>] [--cors <origin>]\n```\n\n| Flag | Default | Description |\n|------|---------|-------------|\n| `--port` | 4096 | HTTP port |\n| `--hostname` | 127.0.0.1 | Bind address |\n| `--cors` | none | CORS origin (repeatable) |\n\n**Authentication** (optional):\n```bash\nOPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=secret opencode serve\nOPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME=custom-user  # default: \"opencode\"\n```\nWhen set, all endpoints require HTTP Basic Auth: `Authorization: Basic <base64(user:pass)>`\n\n## Core Endpoints\n\n### Health\n```\nGET /global/health → {status, version}\n```\n\n### Sessions\n\n**Create session:**\n```\nPOST /session\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"Architecture Chat - docker-sandbox\",\n  \"permission\": [\"read\", \"write\"]\n}\n→ {id, title, ...}\n```\n\n**List sessions:**\n```\nGET /session → [{id, title, ...}]\n```\n\n**Get session:**\n```\nGET /session/:id → {id, title, messages, ...}\n```\n\n**Delete session:**\n```\nDELETE /session/:id\n```\n\n### Messages\n\n**Send message (blocking):**\n```\nPOST /session/:id/message\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Your message here\"}\n  ],\n  \"model\": {\n    \"providerID\": \"anthropic\",\n    \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"\n  }\n}\n→ {info, parts}\n```\n\n**Send message (async, non-blocking):**\n```\nPOST /session/:id/prompt_async\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"...\"}],\n  \"model\": {\"providerID\": \"anthropic\", \"modelID\": \"...\"}\n}\n```\n\n**Abort running session:**\n```\nPOST /session/:id/abort\n```\n\n**List messages:**\n```\nGET /session/:id/message → [{id, role, parts, ...}]\n```\n\n### Streaming (SSE)\n\n**Global event stream:**\n```\nGET /global/event\nAccept: text/event-stream\n```\n\n**Session-scoped event stream:**\n```\nGET /event\nAccept: text/event-stream\n```\n\n**Event format:**\n```\nevent: message.part.updated\ndata: {\"type\":\"message.part.updated\",\"properties\":{...}}\n```\n\n### Event Types\n\n| Event | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `server.connected` | Sent immediately on SSE connect |\n| `session.created` | New session created |\n| `session.updated` | Session metadata changed |\n| `session.deleted` | Session removed |\n| `session.idle` | Session finished processing (response complete) |\n| `session.error` | Session encountered error |\n| `message.updated` | Message metadata changed |\n| `message.part.updated` | **Streaming text delta** — incremental token updates |\n| `message.part.removed` | Message part deleted |\n| `message.deleted` | Full message removed |\n| `permission.asked` | Tool permission request |\n| `permission.response` | Tool permission response |\n| `file.changed` | File modified on disk |\n| `file.watcher.updated` | File watcher state change |\n| `lsp.diagnostics` | LSP diagnostic update |\n\n**Key for streaming:** `message.part.updated` events contain incremental text deltas that should be appended to the current message to display real-time token streaming.\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Get config:**\n```\nGET /config → {providers, models, ...}\n```\n\n**Get available providers/models:**\n```\nGET /config/providers → [{id, models: [...]}]\n```\n\n### Model Selection\n\nModels are specified per-message, not per-session:\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": {\n    \"providerID\": \"anthropic\",\n    \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCommon provider IDs: `anthropic`, `openai`, `google`, `ollama`\n\n**Note:** There are known issues where per-message model selection may be ignored in favor of server defaults (GitHub issue #3517). Test thoroughly.\n\n## Python SDK\n\n```bash\npip install --pre opencode-ai\n```\n\n### Synchronous Usage\n```python\nfrom opencode_ai import Opencode\n\nclient = Opencode(base_url=\"http://localhost:4096\")\n\n# List sessions\nsessions = client.session.list()\n\n# Create session\nsession = client.session.create(title=\"Arch Chat\", permission=[\"read\", \"write\"])\n\n# Send message\nresponse = client.session.prompt(\n    id=session.id,\n    parts=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello\"}],\n    model={\"providerID\": \"anthropic\", \"modelID\": \"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"}\n)\n\n# Stream events\nstream = client.event.list()\nfor events in stream:\n    for event in events:\n        if event.type == \"message.part.updated\":\n            print(event.properties.text, end=\"\", flush=True)\n```\n\n### Async Usage\n```python\nfrom opencode_ai import AsyncOpencode\n\nclient = AsyncOpencode(base_url=\"http://localhost:4096\")\nsessions = await client.session.list()\n```\n\n## Integration Notes for Vista\n\n### Session Mapping\nVista maintains a mapping between its own `ChatSession.id` and OpenCode's session IDs. When creating a Vista chat session with provider \"opencode\", Vista also creates an OpenCode session and stores the mapping.\n\n### Context Assembly\nVista assembles the full prompt (system instructions + diagram context + history + user message) into a single text part before sending to OpenCode. OpenCode does not know about Vista's context structure.\n\n### Streaming Bridge\nVista subscribes to OpenCode's SSE `GET /event` endpoint and translates `message.part.updated` events into Vista's own SSE format (`event: token`) for the browser frontend.\n\n### Health Checking\nUse `GET /global/health` for service health monitoring. Expected response includes server status and version info.\n\n### Lifecycle Management\nVista starts OpenCode via:\n```python\nproc = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(\n    \"opencode\", \"serve\", \"--port\", str(port),\n    stdout=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,\n    stderr=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE\n)\n```\nMonitor process health with periodic `GET /global/health` checks.\n","numLines":237,"startLine":1,"totalLines":237}}}
