{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013rwDbctAuW7ZgEGY77iy62","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Companion WebSocket Bridge Reference\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→The Companion project (forked at https://github.com/ribeec20/claude-websocket-companion) provides a WebSocket bridge between Claude Code CLI and web clients. Vista uses only the **backend** (Bun/Hono server) — not the React frontend.\n     6→\n     7→## Architecture\n     8→\n     9→```\n    10→Vista FastAPI ←→ (WebSocket JSON) ←→ Companion Server ←→ (WebSocket NDJSON) ←→ Claude CLI\n    11→```\n    12→\n    13→The Companion server has two WebSocket endpoints:\n    14→- `/ws/cli/{sessionId}` — Claude CLI connects here (NDJSON protocol)\n    15→- `/ws/browser/{sessionId}` — Vista's backend connects here (JSON protocol)\n    16→\n    17→## Launching Claude CLI\n    18→\n    19→The Companion spawns Claude Code with:\n    20→```bash\n    21→claude --sdk-url ws://localhost:{PORT}/ws/cli/{SESSION_ID} \\\n    22→       --print \\\n    23→       --output-format stream-json \\\n    24→       --input-format stream-json \\\n    25→       --verbose \\\n    26→       -p \"\"\n    27→```\n    28→\n    29→**Critical flags:**\n    30→| Flag | Purpose |\n    31→|------|---------|\n    32→| `--sdk-url` | Hidden flag activating WebSocket mode |\n    33→| `--print` | Headless mode (no terminal UI) |\n    34→| `--output-format stream-json` | NDJSON output |\n    35→| `--input-format stream-json` | NDJSON input |\n    36→| `--verbose` | Enables `stream_event` messages for token streaming |\n    37→| `-p \"\"` | Placeholder prompt (actual prompts via WebSocket) |\n    38→| `--model {model}` | Model selection |\n    39→| `--resume {id}` | Resume previous CLI session |\n    40→| `--dangerously-skip-permissions` | Auto-approve all tool calls |\n    41→\n    42→## WebSocket Protocol\n    43→\n    44→### Browser → Companion (JSON)\n    45→\n    46→**Send user message:**\n    47→```json\n    48→{\n    49→  \"type\": \"user\",\n    50→  \"message\": {\n    51→    \"role\": \"user\",\n    52→    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Your assembled prompt here\"}]\n    53→  }\n    54→}\n    55→```\n    56→\n    57→**Respond to permission request:**\n    58→```json\n    59→{\n    60→  \"type\": \"permission_response\",\n    61→  \"request_id\": \"uuid-from-request\",\n    62→  \"approved\": true,\n    63→  \"original_input\": {\"command\": \"...\"},\n    64→  \"modified_input\": {\"command\": \"...\"}\n    65→}\n    66→```\n    67→\n    68→**Send control request (interrupt, model change):**\n    69→```json\n    70→{\n    71→  \"type\": \"control_request\",\n    72→  \"request_id\": \"generated-uuid\",\n    73→  \"request\": {\n    74→    \"subtype\": \"interrupt\"\n    75→  }\n    76→}\n    77→```\n    78→\n    79→### Companion → Browser (JSON)\n    80→\n    81→**Session initialization (on connect/reconnect):**\n    82→```json\n    83→{\n    84→  \"type\": \"session_init\",\n    85→  \"state\": {\n    86→    \"model\": \"opus\",\n    87→    \"cwd\": \"/path/to/project\",\n    88→    \"tools\": [...]\n    89→  }\n    90→}\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→**Assistant message (complete):**\n    94→```json\n    95→{\n    96→  \"type\": \"assistant\",\n    97→  \"message\": {\n    98→    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    99→    \"content\": [\n   100→      {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Full response text\"}\n   101→    ]\n   102→  }\n   103→}\n   104→```\n   105→\n   106→**Streaming token:**\n   107→```json\n   108→{\n   109→  \"type\": \"stream_event\",\n   110→  \"event\": {\n   111→    \"type\": \"content_block_delta\",\n   112→    \"index\": 0,\n   113→    \"delta\": {\"type\": \"text_delta\", \"text\": \" token\"}\n   114→  }\n   115→}\n   116→```\n   117→\n   118→**Result (response complete):**\n   119→```json\n   120→{\n   121→  \"type\": \"result\",\n   122→  \"cost\": 0.0123,\n   123→  \"session_id\": \"cli-internal-session-id\"\n   124→}\n   125→```\n   126→\n   127→**Permission request (tool approval):**\n   128→```json\n   129→{\n   130→  \"type\": \"permission_request\",\n   131→  \"request_id\": \"uuid\",\n   132→  \"tool_name\": \"Bash\",\n   133→  \"input\": {\"command\": \"ls -la\"}\n   134→}\n   135→```\n   136→\n   137→**Session state update:**\n   138→```json\n   139→{\n   140→  \"type\": \"session_update\",\n   141→  \"state\": {\"model\": \"opus\", \"cwd\": \"...\"}\n   142→}\n   143→```\n   144→\n   145→**Message history (on reconnect):**\n   146→```json\n   147→{\n   148→  \"type\": \"message_history\",\n   149→  \"history\": [\n   150→    {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": {...}},\n   151→    {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": {...}}\n   152→  ]\n   153→}\n   154→```\n   155→\n   156→## Key Integration Points for Vista\n   157→\n   158→### Auto-Approve All Tools\n   159→Since Vista uses `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, no `permission_request` events should arrive. If they do, auto-respond with `approved: true`.\n   160→\n   161→### Session Lifecycle\n   162→1. Vista creates a Companion session (tells it to spawn Claude CLI)\n   163→2. CLI connects via WebSocket to `/ws/cli/{id}`\n   164→3. Vista connects via WebSocket to `/ws/browser/{id}`\n   165→4. Messages flow: Vista → Companion → CLI → Companion → Vista\n   166→5. On session end: Vista closes WebSocket, Companion kills CLI process\n   167→\n   168→### Streaming Translation\n   169→Vista receives `stream_event` with `content_block_delta` from Companion and translates to its own SSE format:\n   170→```\n   171→Companion WS: {\"type\": \"stream_event\", \"event\": {\"type\": \"content_block_delta\", \"delta\": {\"text\": \"tok\"}}}\n   172→Vista SSE:    event: token\\ndata: {\"text\": \"tok\"}\\n\\n\n   173→```\n   174→\n   175→### Reconnection\n   176→- Companion buffers up to 1000 messages for replay\n   177→- On reconnect, Companion sends `session_init` + `message_history`\n   178→- Vista should handle reconnection gracefully if WebSocket drops\n   179→\n   180→### Health Checking\n   181→Companion runs on a known port. Health can be checked via HTTP GET to the server root or a dedicated health endpoint. Monitor process PID for crash detection.\n   182→\n   183→## Companion Server API (HTTP)\n   184→\n   185→| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |\n   186→|----------|--------|---------|\n   187→| `/api/sessions` | GET | List all sessions |\n   188→| `/api/sessions/new` | POST | Create new session + spawn CLI |\n   189→| `/api/sessions/:id` | DELETE | Delete session + kill CLI |\n   190→| `/ws/cli/:id` | WS | CLI WebSocket endpoint |\n   191→| `/ws/browser/:id` | WS | Browser/client WebSocket endpoint |\n   192→\n   193→## Process Management\n   194→\n   195→Companion's `CliLauncher` manages Claude CLI processes:\n   196→- One process per session\n   197→- Monitors process exit codes\n   198→- Supports `--resume` for session recovery\n   199→- Stores session data to `{tmpdir}/vibe-sessions/{id}.json`\n   200→\n   201→Vista's `ServiceLifecycleManager` manages the Companion server process itself:\n   202→- Starts Companion on plugin load\n   203→- Monitors health\n   204→- Auto-restarts on crash with exponential backoff\n   205→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"615fcba1-13a5-40a3-839d-703775331047","uuid":"77eb61ba-f0aa-43a0-bb49-e2ef1e1fab45","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/companion-websocket-reference.md","content":"# Companion WebSocket Bridge Reference\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Companion project (forked at https://github.com/ribeec20/claude-websocket-companion) provides a WebSocket bridge between Claude Code CLI and web clients. Vista uses only the **backend** (Bun/Hono server) — not the React frontend.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nVista FastAPI ←→ (WebSocket JSON) ←→ Companion Server ←→ (WebSocket NDJSON) ←→ Claude CLI\n```\n\nThe Companion server has two WebSocket endpoints:\n- `/ws/cli/{sessionId}` — Claude CLI connects here (NDJSON protocol)\n- `/ws/browser/{sessionId}` — Vista's backend connects here (JSON protocol)\n\n## Launching Claude CLI\n\nThe Companion spawns Claude Code with:\n```bash\nclaude --sdk-url ws://localhost:{PORT}/ws/cli/{SESSION_ID} \\\n       --print \\\n       --output-format stream-json \\\n       --input-format stream-json \\\n       --verbose \\\n       -p \"\"\n```\n\n**Critical flags:**\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `--sdk-url` | Hidden flag activating WebSocket mode |\n| `--print` | Headless mode (no terminal UI) |\n| `--output-format stream-json` | NDJSON output |\n| `--input-format stream-json` | NDJSON input |\n| `--verbose` | Enables `stream_event` messages for token streaming |\n| `-p \"\"` | Placeholder prompt (actual prompts via WebSocket) |\n| `--model {model}` | Model selection |\n| `--resume {id}` | Resume previous CLI session |\n| `--dangerously-skip-permissions` | Auto-approve all tool calls |\n\n## WebSocket Protocol\n\n### Browser → Companion (JSON)\n\n**Send user message:**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user\",\n  \"message\": {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Your assembled prompt here\"}]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Respond to permission request:**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"permission_response\",\n  \"request_id\": \"uuid-from-request\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"original_input\": {\"command\": \"...\"},\n  \"modified_input\": {\"command\": \"...\"}\n}\n```\n\n**Send control request (interrupt, model change):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"control_request\",\n  \"request_id\": \"generated-uuid\",\n  \"request\": {\n    \"subtype\": \"interrupt\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Companion → Browser (JSON)\n\n**Session initialization (on connect/reconnect):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"session_init\",\n  \"state\": {\n    \"model\": \"opus\",\n    \"cwd\": \"/path/to/project\",\n    \"tools\": [...]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Assistant message (complete):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"assistant\",\n  \"message\": {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Full response text\"}\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Streaming token:**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"stream_event\",\n  \"event\": {\n    \"type\": \"content_block_delta\",\n    \"index\": 0,\n    \"delta\": {\"type\": \"text_delta\", \"text\": \" token\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Result (response complete):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"result\",\n  \"cost\": 0.0123,\n  \"session_id\": \"cli-internal-session-id\"\n}\n```\n\n**Permission request (tool approval):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"permission_request\",\n  \"request_id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"Bash\",\n  \"input\": {\"command\": \"ls -la\"}\n}\n```\n\n**Session state update:**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"session_update\",\n  \"state\": {\"model\": \"opus\", \"cwd\": \"...\"}\n}\n```\n\n**Message history (on reconnect):**\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"message_history\",\n  \"history\": [\n    {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": {...}},\n    {\"type\": \"assistant\", \"message\": {...}}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Key Integration Points for Vista\n\n### Auto-Approve All Tools\nSince Vista uses `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, no `permission_request` events should arrive. If they do, auto-respond with `approved: true`.\n\n### Session Lifecycle\n1. Vista creates a Companion session (tells it to spawn Claude CLI)\n2. CLI connects via WebSocket to `/ws/cli/{id}`\n3. Vista connects via WebSocket to `/ws/browser/{id}`\n4. Messages flow: Vista → Companion → CLI → Companion → Vista\n5. On session end: Vista closes WebSocket, Companion kills CLI process\n\n### Streaming Translation\nVista receives `stream_event` with `content_block_delta` from Companion and translates to its own SSE format:\n```\nCompanion WS: {\"type\": \"stream_event\", \"event\": {\"type\": \"content_block_delta\", \"delta\": {\"text\": \"tok\"}}}\nVista SSE:    event: token\\ndata: {\"text\": \"tok\"}\\n\\n\n```\n\n### Reconnection\n- Companion buffers up to 1000 messages for replay\n- On reconnect, Companion sends `session_init` + `message_history`\n- Vista should handle reconnection gracefully if WebSocket drops\n\n### Health Checking\nCompanion runs on a known port. Health can be checked via HTTP GET to the server root or a dedicated health endpoint. Monitor process PID for crash detection.\n\n## Companion Server API (HTTP)\n\n| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |\n|----------|--------|---------|\n| `/api/sessions` | GET | List all sessions |\n| `/api/sessions/new` | POST | Create new session + spawn CLI |\n| `/api/sessions/:id` | DELETE | Delete session + kill CLI |\n| `/ws/cli/:id` | WS | CLI WebSocket endpoint |\n| `/ws/browser/:id` | WS | Browser/client WebSocket endpoint |\n\n## Process Management\n\nCompanion's `CliLauncher` manages Claude CLI processes:\n- One process per session\n- Monitors process exit codes\n- Supports `--resume` for session recovery\n- Stores session data to `{tmpdir}/vibe-sessions/{id}.json`\n\nVista's `ServiceLifecycleManager` manages the Companion server process itself:\n- Starts Companion on plugin load\n- Monitors health\n- Auto-restarts on crash with exponential backoff\n","numLines":205,"startLine":1,"totalLines":205}}}
