{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. The user's request is a ralph planning iteration - they want me to create a detailed implementation plan for the \"architecture-chat\" feature of the Vista plugin. This is iteration 2 (building on iteration 1's plan).\n\n2. The task involves reading task.md, existing plan, progress.txt, domain requirements, specs, architecture diagrams, and all existing source code to produce an improved IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n\n3. I read extensively:\n   - task.md - the planning task description\n   - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md (v1) - the existing 8-phase plan\n   - progress.txt - showing iteration 1 was completed\n   - domain-requirements.md - 8 FRs, TDD candidates\n   - opencode-server-reference.md - REST API + SSE specs\n   - companion-websocket-reference.md - WebSocket protocol + NDJSON reference\n   - All existing source files: app.py, chat_service.py, chat_session_service.py, diagram_watcher.py, provider_service.py, keepalive_manager.py, mcp_server.py, config.py\n   - All route files: chat_sessions.py, architecture.py, chat.py\n   - Models: chat_session.py\n   - Companion fork: index.ts, cli-launcher.ts, routes.ts, session-types.ts, ws-bridge.ts\n   - Architecture diagrams: sequence-claude-chat.mmd, sequence-opencode-chat.mmd, state-service-lifecycle.mmd, data-model.mmd\n   - Frontend: architecture.html (grep for key patterns + SSE section)\n\n4. Serena tools failed because the project root for Serena was different from the working directory. I switched to using Glob/Read/Grep tools directly.\n\n5. I identified key gaps/corrections in the v1 plan:\n   - Companion's WS message type is `user_message` not `user`\n   - Companion uses `--permission-mode` flag not `--dangerously-skip-permissions`\n   - OpenCode uses `prompt_async` + SSE, not blocking `message`\n   - `mcp_server.py` already has `_start_opencode_serve()` - need consolidation\n   - ChatSession model needs `backend_session_id` field\n   - Windows needs `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` for subprocess spawning\n   - `permission_response` uses `behavior: \"allow\"` not `approved: true`\n\n6. I wrote the v2 IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md with all corrections and more detail. Got an error on first Write attempt (\"File has not been read yet\") because the tool requires a fresh read in the same \"session\" - fixed by re-reading the file first.\n\n7. The task requires three final steps: write plan, update progress.txt, and git commit. I completed writing the plan but was interrupted by the summary request before updating progress.txt and committing.\n\nLet me trace the user messages:\n- First user message: The full planning task with context about the architecture-chat feature, including task description, context, key architecture decisions, existing code to understand, deliverable requirements, and current progress from iteration 1.\n- Second user message: Request for detailed conversation summary.\n\nThe pending tasks are:\n- Update progress.txt with iteration 2 info\n- Git commit the plan and artifacts\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user initiated a **ralph planning iteration (iteration 2)** for the \"architecture-chat\" feature of the Vista plugin. The explicit task is to:\n   - Read the task.md, existing v1 plan, progress.txt, domain requirements, architecture specs, and all existing source code\n   - Identify gaps and improvements in the v1 plan\n   - Produce an improved, detailed `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` at `.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n   - Update `progress.txt` with iteration 2 summary\n   - Git commit all changes with message format `plan(architecture-chat-plan): [brief summary]`\n   \n   The feature replaces subprocess-based CLI chat with two protocol-native provider backends: Claude (via Companion WebSocket bridge) and OpenCode (via REST + SSE streaming), with Vista FastAPI as the hub server.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Vista FastAPI Hub Architecture**: Single entry point for all chat communication\n   - **Companion WebSocket Bridge**: Bun/Hono server that bridges Claude CLI via `--sdk-url` WebSocket to browser clients\n   - **OpenCode Server API**: `opencode serve` HTTP REST + SSE streaming for real-time events\n   - **Service Lifecycle Management**: Auto-start/stop/restart Companion and OpenCode with health checks, exponential backoff\n   - **Provider Router Pattern**: Routes messages to correct backend (WebSocket for Claude, REST+SSE for OpenCode)\n   - **watchdog Filesystem Watcher**: Replacing 2s polling with instant filesystem event detection for diagram changes\n   - **Context Assembler**: Extracted prompt assembly module (system prompt + diagram context + history + user message)\n   - **SSE (Server-Sent Events)**: Frontend receives streaming tokens via Vista's SSE endpoint\n   - **Windows-first Platform**: CREATE_NO_WINDOW, taskkill /T /F process tree killing, Bun path discovery\n   - **Session Mapping**: Vista session_id → backend session_id for both providers\n   - **NDJSON Protocol**: Claude CLI's stream-json output format through Companion bridge\n   - **Auto-approve Tool Calls**: `--permission-mode dangerously-skip-permissions` via Companion\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/task.md`**\n     - Source of truth for what to plan. Defines context, architecture decisions, existing code, and deliverable requirements.\n\n   - **`.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`** (WRITTEN - v2)\n     - The main deliverable. Comprehensive 8-phase plan with corrections from v1.\n     - Key corrections: `user_message` WS type, `--permission-mode` flag, `prompt_async` for OpenCode, `backend_session_id` model field, `behavior: \"allow\"` for permission_response.\n     - 8 new files, 9 modified files, 2 removed files planned.\n\n   - **`.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/progress.txt`**\n     - Shows iteration 1 completed. Needs iteration 2 update (PENDING).\n\n   - **`.vista/features/architecture-chat/domain-requirements.md`**\n     - 8 functional requirements (FR-1 through FR-8): Multi-Provider Chat Backend, Companion Integration, OpenCode Integration, Real-Time Diagram Editing, Context Assembly, Model Selection, Service Status Dashboard, Session Management.\n     - TDD candidates: ProviderRouter, ServiceLifecycleManager, ManifestAutoUpdater, ContextAssembler.\n\n   - **`.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/opencode-server-reference.md`**\n     - OpenCode REST API: `POST /session`, `POST /session/:id/prompt_async`, `GET /event` SSE, `GET /global/health`\n     - Event types: `message.part.updated` (streaming tokens), `session.idle` (done), `session.error`\n     - Model selection per-message via `{providerID, modelID}`\n     - Optional HTTP Basic Auth via `OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD`\n\n   - **`.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/companion-websocket-reference.md`**\n     - Companion HTTP API: `POST /api/sessions/create` (was called /new in some docs), `GET /api/sessions`, `DELETE /api/sessions/:id`\n     - WebSocket endpoints: `/ws/cli/{sessionId}` (CLI), `/ws/browser/{sessionId}` (Vista connects here)\n     - Browser sends: `{type: \"user_message\", content: \"...\"}` — NOT `{type: \"user\"}`\n     - Browser receives: `stream_event`, `assistant`, `result`, `permission_request`, `cli_disconnected`\n\n   - **`vista/server/app.py`**\n     - FastAPI app with lifespan managing loop_service, diagram_watcher, keepalive_manager\n     - Imports and includes routers for all routes\n     - Health check at `/api/health`, running loops at `/api/loops/running`\n     - **Planned changes**: Add lifecycle manager start/stop, remove keepalive_manager\n\n   - **`vista/server/services/chat_service.py`**\n     - `ChatService` class with subprocess-based `invoke_provider()` and `invoke_provider_streaming()`\n     - `build_prompt()` static method assembles system prompt + context + history + user message\n     - Windows-specific: `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, `.cmd`/`.bat` handling via `cmd.exe /c`\n     - **Planned changes**: Remove all subprocess logic, delegate to ProviderRouter, keep build_prompt for backward compat\n\n   - **`vista/server/services/chat_session_service.py`**\n     - `ChatSessionService` with CRUD: create, list_sessions, get, delete, add_message, update_name, save\n     - Sessions stored as JSON files under `server/data/sessions/{project_id}/`\n     - Auto-names session from first user message\n     - **No changes needed** (except model field addition)\n\n   - **`vista/server/services/diagram_watcher.py`**\n     - `DiagramWatcher` with 2s polling interval, watches `.mmd` and `.drawio` files\n     - Pub-sub pattern: subscribe/unsubscribe with asyncio.Queue per subscriber\n     - Events: `diagram_added`, `diagram_changed`, `diagram_removed` with file content\n     - **Planned changes**: Replace `_poll_loop()` with watchdog Observer, add debounce, add manifest auto-update\n\n   - **`vista/server/services/provider_service.py`**\n     - `Provider` base class with `get_models()`, `get_invocation()`, `get_chat_cmd()`, `parse_stream_event()`\n     - `ClaudeProvider`: static models [\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"], stream-json parsing\n     - `OpenCodeProvider`: CLI-based model discovery via `opencode models`\n     - `_find_command()` checks PATH + common install locations\n     - `_run_cli_with_timeout()` with Windows CREATE_NO_WINDOW and process tree kill\n     - **Planned changes**: Add live model discovery from running OpenCode server\n\n   - **`vista/server/services/keepalive_manager.py`**\n     - `KeepAliveManager` using tmux panes + file-based messaging via claude_teams\n     - Singleton persistent Claude agent with start/send_message/poll_response/stop\n     - MSYS2 tmux path discovery, orphan cleanup\n     - **Planned: REMOVE entirely** — replaced by WebSocket/SSE via ProviderRouter\n\n   - **`vista/mcp_server.py`**\n     - MCP server entry point using fastmcp 3.x\n     - `_start_opencode_serve()` function at lines 116-144: spawns `opencode serve`, polls health\n     - `app_lifespan`: starts dashboard thread, discovers backends, auto-starts opencode\n     - Ralph tools: ralph_providers, ralph_start, ralph_status, ralph_summary, ralph_stop\n     - Teams tools all commented out\n     - **Planned changes**: Remove `_start_opencode_serve()`, delegate to lifecycle manager\n\n   - **`vista/server/routes/chat_sessions.py`**\n     - Session CRUD endpoints + SSE streaming endpoint\n     - `_stream_response()`: streams from chat_service subprocess to SSE subscribers\n     - `_stream_response_keepalive()`: polls keepalive_manager inbox\n     - SSE merges chat events + diagram watcher events via forwarding queues\n     - `CreateSessionRequest` with mode field (\"oneshot\" | \"persistent\")\n     - **Planned changes**: Remove keepalive logic, use ProviderRouter, simplify to single streaming path\n\n   - **`vista/server/routes/chat.py`**\n     - Blocking `/api/projects/{project_id}/chat` endpoint\n     - **Planned: REMOVE entirely** — superseded by session-based streaming\n\n   - **`vista/server/routes/architecture.py`**\n     - Architecture diagram viewer page + API endpoints\n     - `GET /api/projects/{id}/features/{name}/arch` — manifest\n     - `GET /project/{id}/arch/{name}` — HTML page with chat panel\n     - Passes providers to template\n\n   - **`vista/server/models/chat_session.py`**\n     - `ChatSession` dataclass: id, project_id, feature_name, name, provider, model, messages, team_name\n     - `ChatMessage` dataclass: role, content, timestamp\n     - **Planned changes**: Add `backend_session_id: Optional[str] = None`\n\n   - **`vista/server/config.py`**\n     - `PLUGIN_ROOT`, `DATA_DIR`, `SETTINGS_FILE` paths\n     - `_find_free_port()` in mcp_server.py (not config.py)\n     - `get_server_settings()`, `get_ralph_settings()`, `ensure_full_path()` (Windows registry PATH merge)\n     - **Planned changes**: Add `get_chat_settings()` for companion/opencode config\n\n   - **`vista/companion/web/server/index.ts`**\n     - Bun.serve with Hono app, WebSocket handling\n     - PORT from env var (line 26), CORS on `/api/*`\n     - CLI WebSocket at `/ws/cli/{sessionId}`, Browser at `/ws/browser/{sessionId}`\n     - Auto-relaunch CLI, auto-name sessions, session persistence\n\n   - **`vista/companion/web/server/cli-launcher.ts`**\n     - `CliLauncher.launch()`: creates session, spawns CLI with `--sdk-url`, `--permission-mode`, `--model`, etc.\n     - `spawnCLI()` (line 236): builds args including `--sdk-url ws://localhost:{port}/ws/cli/{sessionId}`\n     - Monitors process exit, persists state\n\n   - **`vista/companion/web/server/routes.ts`**\n     - `POST /sessions/create`: calls `launcher.launch()` with model, permissionMode, cwd, backend\n     - `GET /sessions`: lists all sessions with enriched state\n     - `DELETE /sessions/:id`: kills session\n\n   - **`vista/companion/web/server/session-types.ts`**\n     - Full TypeScript types for CLI ↔ Bridge ↔ Browser protocol\n     - `BrowserOutgoingMessage`: `user_message`, `permission_response`, `interrupt`, `set_model`\n     - `BrowserIncomingMessage`: `session_init`, `stream_event`, `assistant`, `result`, `permission_request`, `error`, `cli_disconnected`\n     - `SessionState` interface with model, cwd, tools, costs, etc.\n\n   - **`vista/server/views/architecture.html`** (read via grep + offset)\n     - SSE connection at line 1172-1213: EventSource to `/api/projects/{id}/chat/sessions/{sid}/stream`\n     - Handles events: `token`, `message_done`, `chat_error`, `diagram_changed`, `diagram_added`, `diagram_removed`\n     - `fetchModels()` at line 955 for dynamic model loading\n     - Chat modes: \"oneshot\" and \"persistent\" toggle\n     - **Planned changes**: Add service status indicators, provider availability, remove persistent mode toggle\n\n   - **Architecture Diagrams Read**:\n     - `sequence-claude-chat.mmd`: Full sequence from session creation through streaming to diagram editing\n     - `sequence-opencode-chat.mmd`: Similar flow using OpenCode REST + SSE\n     - `state-service-lifecycle.mmd`: State machine for service management\n     - `data-model.mmd`: ER diagram with ChatSession, Provider, Feature, ServiceInstance entities\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n   - **Serena tools FileNotFoundError**: Called `mcp__serena__get_symbols_overview` with paths like `server/app.py` but Serena's project root was different from the working directory. Fixed by switching to Glob/Read/Grep tools using full absolute paths.\n   - **Write tool \"File has not been read yet\" error**: Attempted to write IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md but the tool required a fresh read in the current context. Fixed by re-reading the file with `Read` tool (limit=5 lines) before writing.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified 10+ corrections/gaps in the v1 plan by cross-referencing actual source code with plan assumptions\n   - Key protocol mismatch: v1 said `{type: \"user\", message: {role: \"user\", content: text}}` but actual Companion protocol uses `{type: \"user_message\", content: text}` per session-types.ts\n   - Key flag mismatch: v1 referenced `--dangerously-skip-permissions` directly but Companion uses `--permission-mode dangerously-skip-permissions`\n   - Permission response format: v1 said `approved: true` but actual protocol uses `behavior: \"allow\"`\n   - Identified that `mcp_server.py` already has `_start_opencode_serve()` — plan must consolidate, not duplicate\n\n6. All User Messages:\n   - **Message 1**: Full planning task with detailed context:\n     ```\n     **CRITICAL: This is a PLAN iteration. You MUST write a detailed plan.**\n     PROJECT: vista\n     JOB: architecture-chat-plan\n     JOB_DIR: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b\n     ```\n     Includes: Step 0 (understand task), Step 1 (inspect codebase), Step 2 (plan the work), Step 3 (wrap up with plan write, progress.txt update, git commit). Also includes full task description, context references, key architecture decisions, existing code list, deliverable requirements, and current progress from iteration 1.\n   - **Message 2**: Request for detailed conversation summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Update `progress.txt`** with iteration 2 entry (required by task Step 3b)\n   - **Git commit** the plan and artifacts with `git add -A && git commit -m \"plan(architecture-chat-plan): [summary]\"` (required by task Step 3c)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I completed writing the v2 IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to the job directory. The todo list shows \"Update progress.txt and git commit\" as the remaining in_progress task. I was about to:\n   1. Update `progress.txt` at `C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/progress.txt` with iteration 2 entry\n   2. Run `git add -A && git commit -m \"plan(architecture-chat-plan): ...\"` \n   \n   The summary request interrupted this final step.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Complete the mandatory wrap-up steps from the task:\n   - Update `progress.txt` with iteration 2 entry per the format specified in the task:\n     ```\n     ---\n     Iteration: 2 (plan)\n     Time: [timestamp]\n     Plan written to: C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n     Summary: [1-2 sentence summary]\n     ---\n     ```\n   - Git commit with: `git add -A && git commit -m \"plan(architecture-chat-plan): v2 plan with protocol corrections from Companion source code analysis\"`\n   \n   This directly matches the task instruction: \"**You MUST complete ALL of these steps before finishing. Skipping any ste